# ─── OLL Cloudflare Pages / Netlify _redirects ──────────────────────────────
# CRITICAL LESSON FROM THE MAY-2026 INDEXING COLLAPSE (read before editing!)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Cloudflare Pages evaluates `_redirects` rules with status 200 BEFORE doing
# the static-asset lookup. So a rule like `/courses/*  /index.html  200`
# silently CLOBBERS every prerendered file under `build/courses/**/index.html`
# (the SPA homepage shell wins, Google sees duplicate <title>+<meta> across
# ~44 routes, and indexing drops from 11 → 5 pages over the next month).
#
# Therefore: NEVER add a `/foo/*  /index.html  200` rule for any route family
# that has prerendered HTML in `build/` via `scripts/seo-prerender.cjs`.
# If a NEW dynamic family is added later (e.g. blog detail pages), prerender
# its known slugs in `seo-routes.cjs` OR add the SPA fallback ONLY for
# subpaths that have no static counterpart (see /blogs/* below).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Dynamic SPA-only routes (NO prerender) ──────────────────────────────────
# These routes never have a static file in `build/`, so they MUST fall
# through to /index.html for React Router to mount. Each one is a confirmed
# SPA-only path (auth flow, checkout flow, admin area, etc.).
/blogs/*                          /index.html   200
/blog/*                           /index.html   200
/admin/*                          /index.html   200
/admin                            /index.html   200
/login                            /index.html   200
/verify-otp                       /index.html   200
/inquiry                          /index.html   200
/inquiry/*                        /index.html   200

# ── Funnel / checkout / portal flows (SPA-only) ─────────────────────────────
/summer-camp/book                 /index.html   200
/summer-camp/success              /index.html   200
/summer-camp/portal               /index.html   200
/ai-foundations/book              /index.html   200
/ai-foundations/success           /index.html   200
/sm-intern/*                      /index.html   200
/payment/*                        /index.html   200

# ── Authenticated areas (SPA-only, noindex via Helmet) ──────────────────────
/educator-dashboard               /index.html   200
/educator-profile                 /index.html   200
/educator-onboarding              /index.html   200
/educator-onboarding/*            /index.html   200
/educator-interview               /index.html   200
/educator-interview/*             /index.html   200
/educator-apply/*                 /index.html   200
/my-bookings                      /index.html   200
/track-onboarding                 /index.html   200
/track-onboarding/*               /index.html   200
/team-onboarding                  /index.html   200
/team-onboarding/*                /index.html   200
/gp-self-onboarding               /index.html   200
/gp-onboarding-track/*            /index.html   200
/school-tracking                  /index.html   200
/school-tracking/*                /index.html   200
/school-payment-tracker           /index.html   200
/school-payment-tracker/*         /index.html   200
/school-student/*                 /index.html   200
/school-support                   /index.html   200
/support-flow                     /index.html   200
/reports/*                        /index.html   200

# ── DELIBERATE OMISSIONS (these MUST hit the prerendered file): ─────────────
# /courses, /courses/*                  → build/courses/<slug>/index.html
# /school-offerings, /school-offerings/* → build/school-offerings/<cat>/<slug>/index.html
# /summer-camp/skill/*                  → build/summer-camp/skill/<slug>/index.html
# /summer-camp/location/*               → build/summer-camp/location/<slug>/index.html
# /summer-camp/age/*                    → build/summer-camp/age/<slug>/index.html
# /centers, /centers/*                  → static + SPA on detail (Helmet handles)
# /workshops/*                          → build/workshops/<slug>/index.html
# All other top-level pages (/about, /faq, /privacy, /terms, etc.)
#
# Anything NOT in the rules above and NOT a static file will fall through
# to Cloudflare Pages' default SPA behaviour (serve /index.html, status 200).
# Helmet on each component will still set the right meta on hydration.
#
# (The previous `/*  /404.html  404` catch-all did NOT work on Cloudflare
# Pages — random URLs were still returning 200 + SPA shell — and risked
# de-indexing legitimate Google-cached URLs. Removed.)
